  "Question": "\\(\\frac{1000^2}{252^2-248^2}\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(62{,}500\\)",
    "B": "\\(1000\\)",
    "C": "\\(500\\)",
    "D": "\\(250\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\frac12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The denominator is a difference of squares, so factoring avoids calculating the two large squares separately:\n\\[\n252^2-248^2=(252-248)(252+248)=4\\cdot500=2000.\n\\]\nTherefore\n\\[\n\\frac{1000^2}{252^2-248^2}\n=\\frac{1{,}000{,}000}{2000}\n=\\boxed{500},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
